verdict.evidence:
Trace confirms the dead branch. _optimiser_service.py:382-385:

  def _coerce_stopped_terminal_reason(reason: str) -> TerminalReason:
      if reason in TERMINAL_REASON_TO_STATUS:
          return cast(TerminalReason, reason)
      return "cancelled" if reason == "cancelled" else "superseded"

TERMINAL_REASON_TO_STATUS is imported at _optimiser_service.py:98 from _job_lifecycle, where it is defined at _job_lifecycle.py:34-42 as a Mapping with "cancelled" among its KEYS (line 38: "cancelled": CANCELLED_STATUS). Python `in` on a Mapping tests key membership, so `reason in TERMINAL_REASON_TO_STATUS` is True for reason=="cancelled".

Control-flow trace: line 385 executes only on the else path of line 383, i.e. only when reason NOT in TERMINAL_REASON_TO_STATUS. Since "cancelled" IS a key, any reason reaching line 385 necessarily satisfies reason != "cancelled"; thus the ternary test `reason == "cancelled"` is statically False on every reachable path and the expression always yields "superseded". The "cancelled" arm is unreachable. Sole caller _optimiser_service.py:2772 (BackgroundJobStoppedError handler) passes exc.terminal_reason; the return is fed to lifecycle.transition and TERMINAL_REASON_TO_STATUS[...] lookups (line 2780), none of which alters this analysis. Sibling _coerce_worker_terminal_reason (_background_jobs.py:231-242) is the same shape written cleanly (return "error" with no redundant equality re-check), confirming the intended idiom.

